---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReactionNetwork from "../components/ReactionNetwork.astro";
import DigitalLabWorkflow from "../components/DigitalLabWorkflow.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import ResearchArea from "../components/ResearchArea.astro";
import { researchAreas } from "../data/research";
import { technologyGroups } from "../data/projects";
import { organization } from "../data/organization";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Atoms for Humanity | Building a Sustainable Molecular Future"
  description="Atoms for Humanity is a nonprofit research organization building open infrastructure for molecular simulation at massive scale and applying it to sustainable chemistry."
>
  <section class="home-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="hero-wordmark">Atoms for Humanity</p>
        <h1>Building a sustainable molecular future.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Modern civilization is built on chemistry. We develop open-source infrastructure and new scientific methods to discover and design chemistry at scale for human and environmental health.</p>
        <div class="link-row">
          <a class="button button--secondary" href="/work">Explore our work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/about">About Atoms for Humanity <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="container hero-footnote" aria-label="Atoms for Humanity principles">
      <li>MOLECULAR SCIENCE</li><li>OPEN INFRASTRUCTURE</li><li>PUBLIC BENEFIT</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section challenge-section" id="challenge">
    <div class="container split">
      <SectionHeader label="01 — THE CHALLENGE" heading="The chemistry of modern life needs to change." />
      <div class="copy-stack">
        <p> The cornerstones of modern life are built on chemical innovation. Advanced materials, medicines, manufacturing, agriculture, energy systems, and modern technology have all been enabled by breakthroughs in chemistry. But many of the molecular systems we rely on today were optimized for performance and cost without fully accounting for environmental persistence, toxicity, biological compatibility, human health, or long-term sustainability.</p>
        <p>We believe many of these problems can ultimately be addressed at their source: by discovering and designing better chemistry.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--secondary" id="chemical-space">
    <div class="container space-grid">
      <div>
        <SectionHeader label="02 — CHEMICAL SPACE" heading="Finding better chemistry means searching an enormous space." />
        <div class="copy-stack space-copy">
          <p>The space of possible molecules, reactions, catalysts, materials, and chemical processes is vast. Traditional experimental discovery can explore only a small fraction of them.</p>
          <p>Increasing humanity's ability to navigate this space is one of the fundamental requirements for building a more sustainable molecular future.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ReactionNetwork />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section why-now" id="why-now">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        label="03 — WHY NOW"
        heading="A new mode of molecular science is becoming possible."
        intro=" After two centuries of laboratory experimentation, we stand at the threshold of a new era—one in which chemical discovery is becoming computable. Modern computing provides enormous scale. Artificial intelligence increasingly provides the ability to automate scientific reasoning and exploration. Connecting these capabilities creates the possibility of computational experiments operating at scales that were previously impractical."
      />
      <div class="four-grid">
        <article class="concept"><p class="concept-index">01</p><h3>Simulation</h3><p>Ground scientific questions in molecular physics.</p></article>
        <article class="concept"><p class="concept-index">02</p><h3>Compute</h3><p>Run large numbers of calculations in parallel.</p></article>
        <article class="concept"><p class="concept-index">03</p><h3>AI</h3><p>Automate hypothesis generation, analysis, and scientific iteration.</p></article>
        <article class="concept"><p class="concept-index">04</p><h3>Infrastructure</h3><p>Connect these capabilities into a coherent scientific system.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--navy laboratory-section" id="digital-laboratory">
    <div class="container laboratory-grid">
      <div class="laboratory-copy">
        <SectionHeader label="04 — THE DIGITAL LABORATORY" heading="A digital chemical laboratory for humans and AI." />
        <div class="copy-stack">
          <p>Atoms for Humanity is building open infrastructure that allows molecular simulations to be constructed, executed, analyzed, and reproduced at massive scale.</p>
          <p>Human researchers can use this environment to investigate chemical systems systematically. AI systems can use the same scientific tools to formulate hypotheses, run computational experiments, interpret results, and decide what to investigate next.</p>
        </div>
        <blockquote>Give increasingly capable AI access to a massively scalable digital chemical laboratory, and it gains something essential: the ability to test ideas against physical models rather than just propose them.</blockquote>
      </div>
      <DigitalLabWorkflow />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--secondary technology-preview" id="open-infrastructure">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        label="05 — OPEN INFRASTRUCTURE"
        heading="Infrastructure for molecular simulation at scale."
        intro="AFH develops a connected open-source stack spanning scientific data, program interoperability, distributed computation, and cloud access."
      />
      <div class="stack-line" aria-hidden="true"><span>SCIENTIFIC INTENT</span><i></i><span>PHYSICAL COMPUTATION</span></div>
      <div class="technology-groups">
        {technologyGroups.map((project, index) => (
          <article>
            <div class="technology-number">0{index + 1}</div>
            <div>
              <p>{project.category}</p>
              <h3>{project.name}</h3>
              <div class="tech-description">{project.description}</div>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <a class="text-link tech-cta" href="/technology">Explore the technology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section research-section" id="research">
    <div class="container research-grid">
      <div class="research-heading">
        <SectionHeader
          label="06 — RESEARCH"
          heading="Building the tools—and using them to discover new science."
          intro="Infrastructure matters because of the science it enables. AFH develops new computational capabilities alongside an active research program that uses this infrastructure to uncover new science. We open-source all our infrastructure and scientific results."
        />
        <a class="text-link" href="/work">Explore our work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div>
        {researchAreas.map((area) => <ResearchArea area={area} concise />)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--light open-science" id="open-science">
    <div class="container open-grid">
      <SectionHeader light label="07 — OPEN SCIENCE" heading="Scientific capabilities should compound." />
      <div>
        <div class="copy-stack">
          <p>We believe that the power to simulate matter at scale is a fundamental public good and that unlocking this power will lead to transformative progress for human civilization.</p>
          <p>AFH develops open software, workflows, data, protocols, and scientific results so that researchers beyond our organization can use, extend, and improve what we build.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="open-list">
          <li>Open-source scientific software</li>
          <li>Cutting-edge research program</li>
          <li>Shared computational infrastructure</li>
          <li>ChemCloud access for external researchers</li>
          <li>Open scientific workflows and data</li>
          <li>AFH Software Fellows</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="open-note">AFH also provides shared compute and ChemCloud access to external researchers and research groups.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--bright institution-section" id="institution">
    <div class="container institution-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">08 — THE INSTITUTION</p>
        <h2>Building for the long term.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Atoms for Humanity is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit research organization founded to develop and steward scientific infrastructure over long timescales.</p>
        <p>AFH's current research and infrastructure program is supported by a <strong>{organization.support.amount} grant from {organization.support.name}</strong>.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/about">About the organization <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .home-hero { position: relative; padding: clamp(5rem, 9vw, 8rem) 0 0; background: var(--bg-primary); }
  .hero-copy { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; padding-bottom: 1rem; text-align: center; }
  .hero-wordmark { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: var(--blue-primary); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -.025em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .hero-copy h1 { max-width: 1050px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(3.3rem, 6.2vw, 5.9rem); line-height: 1.08; }
  .hero-lede { max-width: 760px; margin: 2rem 0 0; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.6vw, 1.35rem); line-height: 1.6; text-wrap: balance; }
  .hero-copy .link-row { justify-content: center; margin-top: 2.2rem; }
  .hero-footnote { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: clamp(4rem, 7vw, 6rem); margin-bottom: 0; padding: 1.5rem 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--text-muted); font: 500 .75rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); letter-spacing: .075em; list-style: none; }
  .hero-footnote li:last-child { color: var(--green-dark); }
  .challenge-section { padding-block: clamp(5rem, 9vw, 8.5rem); }
  .space-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: center; gap: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem); }
  .space-copy { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .laboratory-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(0, .95fr); gap: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem); align-items: center; }
  .laboratory-copy .copy-stack { max-width: 680px; margin-top: 2rem; }
  blockquote { margin: 2.3rem 0 0; padding: .2rem 0 .2rem 1.5rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--blue-light); color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .stack-line { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 3.5rem; color: var(--text-muted); font: 500 .73rem/1.4 var(--font-sans); letter-spacing: .055em; }
  .stack-line i { height: 1px; flex: 1; background: var(--border); }
  .technology-groups { margin-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .technology-groups article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 65px 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; padding: 2rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .technology-groups article > div:last-child { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, .7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr); gap: .5rem 3rem; }
  .technology-number { padding-top: .15rem; color: var(--text-muted); font: 500 .8rem/1.4 var(--font-sans); }
  .technology-groups p { grid-column: 1; margin: 0; color: var(--text-muted); font: 600 .75rem/1.4 var(--font-sans); letter-spacing: .06em; }
  .technology-groups h3 { grid-column: 1; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); font-weight: 550; }
  .tech-description { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / span 2; align-self: center; max-width: 640px; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .tech-cta { margin-top: 2.2rem; }
  .research-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 7rem); }
  .research-heading { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--header-height) + 3rem); align-self: start; }
  .research-heading .text-link { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .open-grid, .institution-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 7rem); }
  .open-list { list-style: none; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0 1.5rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid #bdcec3; }
  .open-list li { padding: 1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #bdcec3; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1rem; }
  .open-list li::before { content: "·"; margin-right: .6rem; color: var(--green-dark); font-weight: 800; }
  .open-note { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1rem; }
  .institution-grid h2 { margin: 0; }
  .institution-grid > div:last-child > p { margin: 0; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .institution-grid > div:last-child > p + p { margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .institution-grid .text-link { margin-top: 1.8rem; }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .laboratory-grid, .research-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .laboratory-grid { gap: 3rem; }
    .research-heading { position: static; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .hero-copy h1 { max-width: 650px; font-size: clamp(3.3rem, 8.5vw, 4.5rem); }
    .space-grid, .open-grid, .institution-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .technology-groups article > div:last-child { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .tech-description { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; margin-top: .5rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .home-hero { padding-top: 3.5rem; }
    .hero-copy h1 { font-size: clamp(3.1rem, 12vw, 4.3rem); }
    .hero-copy .link-row { align-items: center; flex-direction: column; }
    .hero-wordmark { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .hero-footnote { gap: 1rem; font-size: .66rem; letter-spacing: .035em; }
    .hero-footnote li { max-width: 95px; }
    .hero-footnote li:last-child { text-align: right; }
    .open-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .stack-line span { max-width: 110px; }
    .technology-groups article { grid-template-columns: 30px 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
